<title>USA: Redhook Ale Brewery Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Redhook Ale Brewery Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE, Wash. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							 March 3l,</p>
<p>							  1997	  1996</p>
<p>Sales (includes other sales of</p>
<p> $628,000 and $591,000, respectively) $8,868,210   $8,554,845</p>
<p> Less Excise Taxes			     874,356	833,739</p>
<p> Net Sales				     7,993,854    7,721,106</p>
<p> Cost of Sales				 6,371,882    5,055,061</p>
<p> Gross Profit				  1,621,972    2,666,045</p>
<p> Selling, General and Administrative   2,421,142    1,532,166</p>
<p> Operating Income (Loss)		   (799,170)    1,133,879</p>
<p> Other Income, Net				18,311	257,506</p>
<p> Income (Loss) Before Income Taxes     (780,859)    1,391,385</p>
<p> Provision (Benefit) for Income Taxes  (292,822)	507,855</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)			   (488,037)	883,530</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) Per Share		  (0.06)	   0.10</p>
<p> Avg. Common and Equivalent Shares  (A)7,685,619    9,206,700</p>
<p> Barrels Shipped				  51,400	 49,700</p>
<p>(A)  Excludes common equivalent shares totaling</p>
<p>approximately 1.3 million</p>
<p>shares (primarily convertible preferred stock) due to the anti-dilutive effect when combined with a net loss.</p>
